{
  "id": "ripper-clinic",
  "name": "The Open Hand",
  "description": "A back-room ripperdoc low on the Ribbon, down where the levels barely see daylight: a converted repair shop behind a half-down steel shutter, a red neon open hand in the door's window. In the middle, a salvaged surgical chair in cracked black vinyl with leather straps hanging loose, a ring lamp on a jointed arm over it, a steel instrument trolley half under a green cloth, an IV stand, a plastic curtain on a ceiling rail. Along the back wall, a lit glass cabinet of second-hand chrome (mechanical hands, an eye in a jar, a chrome skull, spinal plates, coiled neural cable), a pale-blue fridge racked with vials of MiraGen script, a violet UV steriliser. On the left, three old monitors with heartbeat traces and a skull scan, a cluttered desk under a warm lamp (a mug, a soldering iron, an ashtray), a steel sink. Hospital-green walls gone stained, pipes and cable overhead, a drain in the floor. A waiting bench by the door with someone's jacket left on it. Clean around the chair, cluttered everywhere else. It's what people get instead of Chiron.",
